From deaf37ee04a174022f891bdd0b1ed94f7b6d8041 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: William Emerison Six <billsix@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 14:16:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] wiki: read the setting through the feature registry in
 the event guide

The listener example in step 4 of wiki/EventSystem.md checks its setting
with CVarGetInteger. Since romhack support (#300) the project's rule is
the opposite: docs/romhacks/DESIGN.md ("Feature rules") says "Code reads
a lockable setting through the registry instead of CVarGet*", and
docs/scripting.md and the header comment of src/port/features/Features.h
say the same. #300 changed the listeners in
src/port/mods/PortEnhancements.cpp accordingly, including the one this
guide is based on, which now reads

    Port_FeatureInt("cheats.pause_exit_whenever", 0)

but the guide was not updated.

A contributor who follows the guide as written adds a cheat or
enhancement that ignores the disable and force rules of the active
romhack and of mounted mods, which is the case the registry exists for.

Change the example to the registry read, say why in one paragraph with a
link to the Feature rules section, and mention that a new setting needs
its row in sDefs in src/port/features/Features.cpp.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 wiki/EventSystem.md | 8 +++++---
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/wiki/EventSystem.md b/wiki/EventSystem.md
index 58a75b6f..6bec3416 100644
--- a/wiki/EventSystem.md
+++ b/wiki/EventSystem.md
@@ -58,14 +58,16 @@ CALL_CANCELLABLE_EVENT(RenderPauseCourseOptions, &canPause) {
 ---
 
 ## 4. Create the Listener (Callback)
-Implement the logic that reacts to the event. This is usually where you check for CVars or custom mod logic.
+Implement the logic that reacts to the event. This is usually where you check a setting or custom mod logic.
+
+Read a setting through the feature registry (`Port_FeatureInt`), not through its CVar. A romhack or mod can disable a feature or force its value, and only a read through the registry honours that; see [Feature rules](../docs/romhacks/DESIGN.md#feature-rules). A new setting also needs its row in `sDefs` in `src/port/features/Features.cpp`.
 
 **File:** `src/port/mods/PortEnhancements.c`
 
 ```c
 void OnRenderPauseCourseOptions(IEvent* event) {
-    // Only apply the logic if the specific CVar is enabled
-    if (CVarGetInteger("gPauseExitWhenever", 0) == 0) {
+    // Only apply the logic if the feature is enabled
+    if (Port_FeatureInt("cheats.pause_exit_whenever", 0) == 0) {
         return;
     }
 

